WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.043
- All right, everybody,

00:00:01.043 --> 00:00:03.480
let's squeeze in one more
story before we say goodbye.

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.313
I love this story.

00:00:04.313 --> 00:00:05.282
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.282 --> 00:00:08.220
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.290
It's never too late to follow your dreams.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.420
We hear that phrase all the time,

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.220
and sometimes it feels like empty words,

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.810
but not with this next story, y'all.

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:18.900
This is Shamone and she is a mama of four.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.020
And two years ago, her
niece had a medical question

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.850
which Shamone tried to answer.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.410
That interaction actually awakened

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:28.110
an old desire in her to become a doctor.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.180
But instead of pushing
her dream back down,

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.160
this time Shamone acted on it.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.863
Today, at the ripe age of 43,

00:00:33.863 --> 00:00:36.720
Shamone is in her first
year of medical school,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:37.710
which is so cool.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.570
Let's get this boss mama in here.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.370
This was a dream, right?

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.420
That just never went away.
- Absolutely.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:46.530
Yes, absolutely.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:51.030
You know, fear can sometimes
stop us from doing things.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:54.750
And so, the MCAT is the test that we need

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:56.820
to get into medical school,

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.820
and it stopped me in
my tracks 15 years ago.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:07.140
And now, in my second
semester of medical school,

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.030
it is very exciting.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.650
- I love this.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.390
I'm not only happy for you.

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:15.510
I'm happy that you're this
light to other people right now

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.250
sitting at home going, "Man,
I always wanna do this.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.083
Why don't I do this?"

00:01:18.083 --> 00:01:20.040
And we always feel like
we age out of something

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.410
and you can't age outta
something until you die.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:25.620
So, keep doing what you wanna
do until that last breath.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.840
So there's another important
reason that you're doing this.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.100
Can you share that?

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:29.933
- Sure.

00:01:29.933 --> 00:01:34.110
You know, COVID really was
tough for African Americans.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.220
It was tough for everyone,

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.500
but we suffered even more.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.500
And some of it has to
do with our hesitancy

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.440
in going to the positions,
going to our doctors.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.840
And it's legitimate,

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.320
but my goal and my hope
is that I can kinda act

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:53.340
like a bridge between my
community and the medical field,

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:56.460
because the more we go to our physicians,

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.110
have a relationship with our physicians,

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:01.020
the better we can do
overall in our health.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:01.853
- Absolutely.

00:02:01.853 --> 00:02:04.230
You trust the physician with your health

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:06.750
and then you also can catch stuff in time.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.670
That's the the most important thing.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:09.930
Thank you so much, Shamone.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:10.763
I'm so proud of you.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:11.596
I don't even know you,

00:02:11.596 --> 00:02:12.429
but I'm so proud of you.

00:02:12.429 --> 00:02:14.130
You're so cool.
- Thank you.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:18.180
- Congratulations on just
this awakening of this dream.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.110
I'm so stoked for you.

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:21.417
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:21.417 --> 00:02:24.000
(audience cheering)

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.050
And that's not all, ma'am.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.450
Our season-long partner,
Pilot, pen makers of G2,

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:29.040
the go-to pen of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.740
want to honor inspiring
people just like you, ma'am.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:32.730
So they're gonna be writing you a check

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.710
for $1,000 to help out with some bills.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:35.717
(audience cheering)

00:02:35.717 --> 00:02:38.457
- What? (laughing)

00:02:38.457 --> 00:02:41.515
- Thank you so much, Shamone!
- No, thank you!

00:02:41.515 --> 00:02:42.773
Thank you.

00:02:42.773 --> 00:02:44.550
- All right, thank you
to all our guests today.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.726
Ana Gasteyer, Phil Dunster, Rizz, Farrah,

00:02:47.726 --> 00:02:49.163
and Devon Gilfillian.

00:02:49.163 --> 00:02:49.996
Y'all have a great day,

00:02:49.996 --> 00:02:50.829
and if it's not, try and change it.

